              "id": "kafka-rabbitmq-step-1",
              "title": "Publish, deliver and confirm",
              "description": "Imagine a customer placing an order. The store (the producer) sends a message, and another part of the system (the consumer or worker) acts on it. A single arrow shows where the message goes. Where you see two arrows, one shows delivery and the other shows the worker reporting back. Kafka saves where each group stopped reading. RabbitMQ removes a job after the worker confirms it is done. Redis marks the job as done for that group and keeps the original message in the stream.",
